WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.516
MCP A Creator and the One Hub:

2
00:00:02.396 --> 00:00:08.925
one solution for a question no office can answer today. What does a weapon system really cost?

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:16.604
The Department of Defense plans to spend more than 2.4 trillion dollars on its costliest weapon programs,

4
00:00:16.484 --> 00:00:20.118
and has gone nine years without a clean audit opinion.

5
00:00:20.298 --> 00:00:23.636
For one aircraft carrier, four official costs disagree.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.747
Our answer has four layers: a creator that builds MCP servers,

7
00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:32.748
servers that read the public record, an agent environment,

8
00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:36.109
and a financial-control layer no model can override.

9
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:45.294
It runs today as seven Databricks apps, deployed from GitHub with one command: six MCP servers, with 63 tools.

10
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:50.288
MCP A Creator turns a question and a table into a tested,

11
00:00:50.168 --> 00:00:55.824
governed server. Fifteen of fifteen generated projects pass their own tests.

12
00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:01.920
The front center is where people use it. The Position page shows which figure to quote,

13
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.084
and walks from the cap to the budget, every number cited to its page.

14
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:08.913
Here an agent works a live question.

15
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.842
The orchestrator routes it to a specialist. Code packs the records in exact decimals,

16
00:01:14.722 --> 00:01:17.785
a model explains, and code checks every number.

17
00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:22.738
The agent only proposes. This user holds the program office role,

18
00:01:22.618 --> 00:01:26.955
so the app refuses the proposal that Financial Operations owns.

19
00:01:27.135 --> 00:01:29.062
Unity Catalog makes that call.

20
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:35.219
Ask the evidence orchestrates three MCP servers for one answer, and names every call.

21
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:47.818
Every figure is analyzed, reconciled, cited and gated by code. 7,743 of 7,746 budget tie-outs pass.

22
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:53.438
On an outside evaluator's questions, Claude answered 83 percent

23
00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:59.492
with these servers, and 10 percent without. 1,770 tests pass from a clean clone.

24
00:02:00.217 --> 00:02:03.158
The next program brings its data, not new software.

25
00:02:03.338 --> 00:02:08.332
AI builds and explains. Code proves the number. The owning role decides.

